; TRIALS MODE — the module's own default artwork, as actions
;
; Generated by tools/make-trials-sff.py. Edit that, not this.
;
; Every action here is one frame of one sprite in trials.sff, held indefinitely. They
; exist so that a Trials Config key can name artwork as `anim = N` rather than as
; `spr = group, index` — see the COMMAND GLYPHS and STEP BACKGROUNDS blocks in
; system.def. The module's shipped defaults use `spr`, because that route needs no
; action lookup at all; `anim` is here for a screenpack that wants to animate the
; module's own sprites without shipping an sff of its own.
;
; A screenpack's own `anim = N` means an action in ITS air, not one below. Which file a
; number is resolved against follows whoever wrote the key, exactly as the coordinate
; space does.

; block background, vertical Layout — 270x104
[Begin Action 0]
0,0, 0,0, -1

; block background, horizontal Layout — 280x36
[Begin Action 1]
0,1, 0,0, -1

; Step background, vertical Layout — 250x9
[Begin Action 2]
0,10, 0,0, -1

; Step background body, horizontal Layout (stretched) — 4x9
[Begin Action 3]
0,20, 0,0, -1

; Step background tail, horizontal Layout — 4x9
[Begin Action 4]
0,21, 0,0, -1

; Step background head, horizontal Layout — 6x9
[Begin Action 5]
0,22, 0,0, -1
